<p>Australia announced a three-month cut to its fuel excise, lowering the tax by about 26 Australian cents per litre, after oil prices jumped and fuel strains spread across the country amid the war involving Iran. Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said the move is meant to keep fuel within reach for households and businesses, while national and state leaders also discussed ways to respond to shortages and price pressure. States added their own relief measures. Victoria and Tasmania made public transport free for a limited period, hoping to get more commuters out of cars and ease demand for petrol. Federal officials also tried to reassure the public that fuel shipments were still arriving, saying shortages in some rural towns reflected panic buying and distribution bottlenecks rather than a full break in supply. The response shows how a conflict far from Australia is already affecting daily life there, from household transport costs to fuel access in regional areas. It also shows governments at several levels moving quickly to soften the blow for commuters and reduce pressure on fuel demand.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/x0IeT_PHhDuOrr-bu5hR053cDzJkHrlLDxyF3HA_gTY7yXmSnaMGTSBvUQQcU5sKyNRxHyq_YBfO-GcCuNA2cjcFiszLVXP_p-49pgR4p2Kl' alt='Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese speaks to the media during a press conference at Parliament House in Canberra, Australia, 30 March, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cost to budget: Officials said the three-month tax cut will cost the federal government about A$2.55bn, or roughly $1.75bn, in lost revenue.</li><li>Oil benchmark: Al Jazeera reported crude oil rose above $116 a barrel as the broader energy crisis deepened, adding to pressure on Australian pump prices.</li><li>Emergency powers: Australia&#x27;s parliament introduced a bill that would let the government underwrite purchases of shiploads of fuel to boost domestic supply.</li><li>Stock coverage: Officials cited data showing Australia held 39 days of petrol supply as authorities weighed more steps to stabilize distribution.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Anthony Albanese: The prime minister cast the excise cut as immediate relief for households and urged Australians to drive less as pressure grew in regional communities. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986754/australia-to-halve-fuel-tax-to-keep-prices-within-reach-of-citizens-amid-iran-war'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Victorian and Tasmanian governments: Both state governments chose free public transport as a practical way to cut demand, hoping to reduce city driving and fuel use while still giving commuters a workable way to travel. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c937n0yxggeo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>New South Wales government: Authorities pointed to mounting pressure on service stations in parts of the state as shortages spread, with particular concern for rural communities if conditions worsen. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986754/australia-to-halve-fuel-tax-to-keep-prices-within-reach-of-citizens-amid-iran-war'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>New York Times analysis: The paper described the free-transit moves in Victoria and Tasmania as a sign of how sharply the oil shock tied to the war in Iran has reached places far from the conflict itself. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/30/world/australia/australia-melbourne-free-transit.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/mar/30/australia-politics-live-national-cabinet-fuel-prices-oil-crisis-labor-anthony-albanese-chris-bowen-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb'>Labor backs Greens inquiry into gas export tax – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/30/world/australia/australia-melbourne-free-transit.html'>In Australia, Victoria and Tasmania Waive Transit Fares as Fuel Prices Soar</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c937n0yxggeo'>Fuel tax halved and free public transport offered as war pushes up prices in Australia</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986754/australia-to-halve-fuel-tax-to-keep-prices-within-reach-of-citizens-amid-iran-war'>Australia to halve fuel tax to keep prices within reach of citizens amid Iran war</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/30/australia-to-halve-fuel-tax-as-global-energy-crisis-deepens'>Australia to halve fuel tax as global energy crisis deepens</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>